<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Study Habits for Success</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning to Manage Time</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Compose a detailed personal narrative. Interactive: Compile feedback for collaborative writing in a structured manner.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a detailed narrative about a personal study experience, including reflections on what worked and what could be improved (e.g., "Last month, I realized I was falling behind in math. I started setting reminders to review my notes every day after dinner. Now, I feel more confident when solving equations."). Can contribute to a collaborative guide on study strategies by organizing peer feedback and adding recommendations (e.g., "Peers have suggested writing down homework in an agenda to avoid missing deadlines. Others have recommended setting phone reminders."). Can compile and paraphrase feedback on study habits during peer review sessions and organize it into a report (e.g., "The feedback suggests that making a study schedule and using color-coded notes improves time management.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 34%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e6f2f9; color: #1a5276; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher asks students to think about their own study habits and write down three sentences. One sentence should describe a habit they *used to* have, and two sentences should describe habits they *have developed* for better time management. Students quickly share one sentence with a partner. Example: "I used to procrastinate on assignments. Now, I have developed a routine to complete homework every day after dinner. I have also learned to prioritize tasks effectively."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes on the board, modeling the use of "used to" and "have developed" with examples related to "study," "time," and "management." The teacher explicitly uses vocabulary such as "procrastinate," "improve," "achievements," and "routines." The teacher models the pronunciation of /d/ in "improved" and /t/ in "accomplished."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say, 'I used to study late at night,' does it mean I still study late now?" (Expected answer: "No, you don't anymore.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say, 'I have developed a new strategy,' does it mean it's a past action with current results, or just a past action?" (Expected answer: "Past action with current results/impact.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Study Habits for Success."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Students are given a short narrative excerpt (approx. 100-120 words) from a student describing their journey with time management for "study habits." The text will be titled "My Path to Productive Study." It will be rich in target vocabulary (e.g., "goals," "strategies," "focus," "achievements," "improvement") and grammar (Present Perfect, Past Simple). The register is informal but reflective.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpret and analyze written texts on academic and personal development to identify key strategies and reflections on "time management" and "study habits."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> Students read the text quickly and answer: "What is the main message the writer wants to convey about their study experience?" (Focus: overall "improvement" and "progress").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases describing "past habits" (e.g., "I used to feel overwhelmed by assignments") with "current achievements" (e.g., "I have learned to prioritize my tasks"). They will identify sentences using Present Perfect and Past Simple.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences and short paragraphs using the Present Perfect for "achievements" and Past Simple for "reflecting" on past "habits." They will utilize target vocabulary (nouns: "goals," "strategies," "productivity," "improvement," "management"; verbs: "manage," "procrastinate," "develop," "achieve," "organize"; adjectives: "effective," "focused," "consistent").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice (Sentence Transformation):</b> Students rewrite sentences, changing "past habits" into "current achievements" using "used to" and "have developed/improved."
                        Example: "I didn't plan my study time well." -> "I used to struggle with planning my study time, but now I have developed an effective schedule." Or "I often forgot assignments." -> "I used to forget assignments, but I have improved my organization by setting reminders every day." (Focus on writing accuracy).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-Controlled Practice (Guided Paragraph Writing):</b> The teacher provides sentence starters and WH-questions (e.g., "What did you used to do?", "What have you done to improve?", "How has this helped your grades?") to guide students in writing a short paragraph (3-4 sentences) about a specific aspect of their "study habits" and "time management." Students must integrate at least two vocabulary words from the list.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Check & Initial Feedback:</b> Students exchange their guided paragraphs with a partner. Each student reads their partner's paragraph and identifies one sentence using the Present Perfect and one using the Past Simple. They also identify one instance of target vocabulary. Partners provide brief written feedback on clarity or grammatical correctness (e.g., "Check verb tense here," "Good use of 'strategy'"). The teacher reminds students to pronounce -ed endings correctly if they discuss their feedback orally.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Study Habits for Success."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual Writing Product (Personal Narrative) followed by Collaborative Writing Input (Compiling Feedback).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Personal Narrative Composition (Individual):</b> Students compose a detailed personal narrative (120-150 words) about their own "study experience" and "time management" journey. The narrative must include:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">An introduction to a past "habit" or challenge (using Past Simple, e.g., "I used to struggle with completing assignments on time.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Specific actions or "strategies" they "have developed" or "improved" (using Present Perfect, e.g., "I have set clear goals," "I have learned to prioritize tasks.").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Reflection on the positive "results" or "achievements" (e.g., "My grades have improved significantly").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of at least 5 target vocabulary words (e.g., "management," "focus," "productivity," "effort," "success").</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two complex sentences using adverbs of frequency (e.g., "I always review," "I sometimes feel").</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Peer Review for Collaborative Guide (Interactive Writing):</b> Students exchange their completed narratives with a new partner. Each partner acts as a "reviewer" and identifies two strong points and two suggestions for "improvement" in their partner's narrative, specifically focusing on "time management" techniques or "study strategies." They write these suggestions down in a structured format (e.g., "My peer suggests [strategy] to manage time effectively. They also recommend [another strategy]."). This feedback will be compiled in the next stage. This activity embodies the sociolinguistic aspect of "negotiating plans and sharing experiences."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation during peer review, collection of personal narratives and peer feedback forms, and a simple rubric for narrative writing and feedback compilation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their personal narrative and the peer feedback form they completed for their partner. They then spend 3-5 minutes reviewing the feedback they received for their own narrative.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (for the narrative and feedback):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and Cohesion of Narrative (organization, flow of ideas).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate use of Present Perfect for "achievements" and Past Simple for "past habits."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target "vocabulary" related to "study habits" and "time management."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Quality and relevance of peer "feedback" (clear suggestions, constructive tone).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effort in compiling "feedback" in a "structured manner" (as demonstrated on the feedback sheet).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following prompts on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One specific thing I learned about writing a detailed narrative today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one effective study strategy I read in my peer's narrative or received as feedback that I might try?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has my ability to express personal 'achievements' and 'past habits' in writing improved today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What challenges did I face when trying to organize my thoughts into a detailed narrative or when giving structured 'feedback'?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in promoting the writing of detailed narratives and the compilation of feedback? (e.g., "The guided paragraph writing in Stage 3 effectively prepared students for the main task." or "Students engaged well with peer review, especially when given a clear structure for feedback.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson to further support students in organizing and summarizing information for the collaborative guide? (e.g., "Some students struggled with paraphrasing feedback; I might provide sentence frames next time." or "More explicit examples of how to compile diverse feedback into a cohesive report are needed.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 5: Mediation & Integration), students will use the collected and compiled peer feedback to create a collaborative "Study Strategies Guide." They will mediate information from their own narratives and their peers' feedback to summarize and present key "time management" and "study habits" recommendations to the class, thus integrating all learned skills.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">[Date]</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>